  "metadata": {
    "purpose": "Govern end-to-end delivery workflows for agent-runner-v2, a Python 3.11+ LLM workflow orchestration engine with advanced complexity. This SOP establishes state machine enforcement, approval gates, agent role boundaries, and document-first execution discipline for reliable multi-step delivery pipelines with AI agent orchestration (Claude, Codex, Qwen, DeepSeek), review loops, and human-in-the-loop approval.",
    "core_principle": "Document-Driven + State-Driven Execution. All workflow progression is determined by artifact state and runner-enforced transitions, never by prompt-driven ad-hoc decisions. Artifacts are the single source of truth; the runner reads and enforces them. meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel between agents and runner.",
    "authority_precedence": [
      "Runner Logic — executable state machine enforcement, timeouts, routing, sidecar validation, coder timeout enforcement",
      "SOP/Status Rules — canonical workflow definition and transition rules",
      "Artifact Metadata — status, approval, supersession links (from meta.json sidecar)",
      "Artifact Body Content — detailed findings, implementation details",
      "Note: Approval is runner-enforced via status transitions, not artifact-defined"
    ],
    "project_complexity_level": "Advanced",
    "recommended_workflow_scope": "All delivery templates (Initiative, Plan, Task Graph, Task, Implementation Plan, Review, Validation, Memory) + full agent system (8 roles + Runner) + multi-coder support + model aliasing",
    "key_constraints": [
      "meta.json sidecar is ONLY communication channel; no stdout JSON parsing, no fallback recovery",
      "No phase skipping; strict state machine enforcement by runner",
      "No overwriting approved artifacts; must use supersession with explicit links",
      "Agent master prompts are deprecated; workflow configs in template_groups.py serve as contracts",
      "Cross-project support via --target-project-root for scaffolding into other repositories",
      "Model alias resolution via model_mapping.json for coder abstraction",
      "Coder timeout enforcement via AGENT_RUNNER_CODER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS env var (default 600s)"
    ]
  },
  "workflow_states": [
    {"name": "INITIATIVE_CREATED", "owner": "Planner", "artifact": "Initiative", "description": "Draft submitted; awaiting Architect review for scope, feasibility, stakeholder alignment"},
    {"name": "INITIATIVE_APPROVED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Initiative", "description": "Approved; planning may commence"},
    {"name": "PLAN_DRAFT", "owner": "Planner", "artifact": "Plan", "description": "Plan drafted with phases, milestones, gates; awaiting review"},
    {"name": "PLAN_APPROVED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Plan", "description": "Approved; task decomposition may commence"},
    {"name": "TASK_GRAPH_DRAFT", "owner": "Task Decomposer", "artifact": "Task Graph", "description": "Task graph drafted with dependencies; awaiting review"},
    {"name": "TASK_GRAPH_APPROVED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Task Graph", "description": "Approved; execution may commence"},
    {"name": "TASK_PENDING", "owner": "Executor", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Created; dependencies met; awaiting execution start"},
    {"name": "TASK_IN_PROGRESS", "owner": "Executor", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Being executed; collecting evidence"},
    {"name": "TASK_IMPLEMENTED", "owner": "Executor", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Implementation complete; awaiting Review + Validation + Architect approval"},
    {"name": "REVIEW_FINAL", "owner": "Reviewer", "artifact": "Review", "description": "Review complete with APPROVED or REJECTED decision"},
    {"name": "VALIDATION_FINAL", "owner": "Validator", "artifact": "Validation", "description": "Validation complete with APPROVED or REJECTED decision"},
    {"name": "TASK_APPROVED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Approved after Review Final (APPROVED) AND Validation Final (APPROVED); counts toward completion"},
    {"name": "COMPLETED", "owner": "Runner", "artifact": "Delivery", "description": "Terminal state; all in-scope tasks APPROVED; no rejections"},
    {"name": "TASK_BLOCKED", "owner": "Executor", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Blocked by dependency, resource, or unresolved issue; requires intervention"},
    {"name": "TASK_FAILED", "owner": "Executor", "artifact": "Task", "description": "Execution failed; error, timeout, or irrecoverable issue"},
    {"name": "INITIATIVE_REJECTED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Initiative", "description": "Terminal state; rejected at intake or planning"},
    {"name": "SUPERSEDED", "owner": "Architect", "artifact": "Any", "description": "Terminal state; artifact superseded by newer version with explicit link"}
  ],
  "workflow_approval_authority": {
    "initiative_gate": "Architect approves INITIATIVE_CREATED → INITIATIVE_APPROVED",
    "plan_gate": "Architect approves PLAN_DRAFT → PLAN_APPROVED",
    "task_graph_gate": "Architect approves TASK_GRAPH_DRAFT → TASK_GRAPH_APPROVED",
    "implementation_plan_gate": "Architect approves IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_DRAFT → IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_APPROVED",
    "task_approval_gate": "Architect approves TASK_IMPLEMENTED → TASK_APPROVED (requires REVIEW_FINAL APPROVED + VALIDATION_FINAL APPROVED)",
    "review_authority": "Reviewer finalizes and approves/rejects REVIEW_DRAFT → REVIEW_FINAL",
    "validation_authority": "Validator finalizes and approves/rejects VALIDATION_DRAFT → VALIDATION_FINAL",
    "binding_principle": "Approval is durable once recorded in meta.json sidecar; execution does not grant approval; supersession required for changes"
  },
  "description": "WORKFLOW_SOP_v1.0 — agent-runner-v2 Delivery SOP (Advanced Complexity). Complete specification for document-driven, state-driven delivery orchestration with 8 agent roles, multi-coder support, strict phase ordering, meta.json sidecar communication, and durable supersession tracking. Full markdown content preserved in docs/delivery/00_templates/ folder."\n\n**Document Type:** SOP  \n**Version:** v1.0  \n**Status:** Active  \n**Owner:** Architect  \n**Project Complexity:** Advanced  \n**Last Updated:** 2026-06-04  \n**Applies to:** LLM Workflow Orchestration Engine (agent-runner-v2)  \n**Upstream Specs:** UKBE_Artifact_v1_FINAL.md, UKBE_Contract_Builder_v1.1_FINAL.md, UKBE_Core_Data_Model_v1.2.1_FINAL.md\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis SOP governs the end-to-end delivery workflow for agent-runner-v2—a complex Python 3.11+ LLM orchestration engine supporting multi-coder (Claude, Codex, Qwen, DeepSeek), multi-model, multi-phase delivery with advanced review loops and human-in-the-loop approval gates. It establishes:\n\n1. **Workflow state machine** and phase transitions (no skipping, no out-of-order execution)\n2. **Complete artifact lifecycles** (Initiative → Plan → Task Graph → Tasks → Review → Validation → Memory → Completed)\n3. **Nine agent roles with exclusive authority boundaries** (Planner, Task Decomposer, Implementation Planner, Executor, Reviewer, Validator, Memory Manager, Architect, Runner)\n4. **Document-first, state-driven execution** (never prompt-driven; artifacts define contracts, not prompts)\n5. **meta.json sidecar communication protocol** (ONLY channel between agents and runner; no stdout JSON parsing, no silent recovery)\n6. **Independent validation philosophy** (Reviewer ≠ Executor ≠ Validator; structured decision records)\n7. **Multi-coder parallel execution** with model aliasing and budget enforcement\n8. **Supersession and memory management** for durable, auditable delivery context and multi-initiative lineage\n\nThis SOP is **binding on all agents, runners, and architects** executing delivery workflows in agent-runner-v2. Deviations require explicit architectural amendment recorded in meta.json."\n\n---\n\n## Core Principle: Document-Driven + State-Driven Execution\n\n**Not prompt-driven. Not stdout-parsed. Not silently recovered. Explicit. Durable. Enforceable.**\n\nDelivery is executed through:\n\n- **Artifacts** (Initiative, Plan, Task Graph, Task, Implementation Plan, Review, Validation, Memory) that embody explicit decisions, scope, and contracts\n- **State machines** that enforce phase order, no skipping, no overwriting approved artifacts\n- **meta.json sidecars** that carry durable proof of execution, approval, and decision context\n- **Agent role boundaries** (defined in `08_agents/` and `template_groups.py`) that lock scope and prevent drift\n- **Runner logic** that enforces SOP rules, budgets, timeouts, and state transitions\n\n**Templates define contracts** (workflow step configurations in `template_groups.py` are agent invocation contracts). **Agent master prompts are deprecated.** Agent role files in `08_agents/` define boundaries and handoff rules only, not prompt content.\n\n## Project-Specific SOP Constraints (agent-runner-v2)\n\n- **meta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel** between agents and runner. No stdout JSON parsing. No fallback recovery. Sidecar structure is schema v2 JSON.\n- **No pre-invocation sidecar writes** by the runner. Agents are responsible for creating and updating sidecars as they complete work.\n- **No markdown write-backs** (`sync_review_metadata`, `stamp_created_metadata`, etc.). Sidecar is the single source of truth; markdown is for human readability only.\n- **Explicit exception routing** — hard failures route immediately via `route_after_failure()`. No disk recovery functions. No silent fallback.\n- **Reviewer and Executor MUST be different agents.** No one can review their own implementation.\n- **Validator MUST be different from both Reviewer and Executor.** Independent final validation is mandatory.\n- **Architect holds exclusive approval authority** for all major gates (Initiative, Plan, Task Graph, Implementation Plan, final Task approval).\n- **Model aliasing support** for multiple coders (Claude via `ukbe-run-agent`, Codex/OpenAI, Qwen, DeepSeek) with fallback policy defined in runner config.\n- **Upstream UKBE specs** (Artifact v1, Contract Builder v1.1, Core Data Model v1.2.1) inform but do not override this SOP. Runner logic is authoritative.\n\n---\n\n## Authority Precedence (Strict Hierarchy)\n\nWhen conflicts arise, resolution follows this hierarchy (highest to lowest):\n\n1. **Runner Logic** — State enforcement, budget checks, routing, sidecar validation, timeout handling, phase ordering\n2. **SOP + Status Rules** — This document (WORKFLOW_SOP_v1.0) and DELIVERY_STATUS_RULES_v1.md\n3. **Artifact Metadata** (meta.json sidecar) — Approval status, decision, evidence, upstream refs, timestamps\n4. **Artifact Body Content** — Initiative text, plan scope, task description, review findings\n\n**Implication**: The SOP overrides artifact content. The runner enforces the SOP. Approval is durable: once locked, scope changes require new artifacts + supersession links + re-approval.\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Approval Authority\n\n**Approval is runner-enforced, not artifact-defined.**\n\n- **Runner** reads approval decisions from **meta.json sidecars only** (no stdout JSON fallback, no markdown write-back, no disk recovery)\n- **Architect** holds **exclusive approval authority** for Initiative, Plan, Task Graph, Implementation Plan, and final Task approval\n- **Reviewer** holds authority for Review artifacts (independent validation of implementations)\n- **Validator** holds authority for Validation artifacts (final behavior/contract verification)\n- **Execution ≠ Approval**: An agent executing a task does not approve the task; only the designated authority (Architect/Reviewer/Validator) approves\n- **Hard failures route immediately** via `route_after_failure()` to Architect (no silent recovery)\n\n---\n\n## Workflow State Machine\n\n### Full State Diagram\n\n```\nINITIATIVE_CREATED\n    ↓ (Planner drafts)\nINITIATIVE_APPROVED (Architect)\n    ↓\nPLAN_DRAFT\n    ↓ (Planner drafts)\nPLAN_REVIEWED (Reviewer assessment)\n    ↓\nPLAN_APPROVED (Architect)\n    ↓\nTASK_GRAPH_DRAFT\n    ↓ (Task Decomposer drafts)\nTASK_GRAPH_REVIEWED (Reviewer assessment)\n    ↓\nTASK_GRAPH_APPROVED (Architect)\n    ↓\nTASK_PENDING → TASK_IN_PROGRESS → TASK_IMPLEMENTED\n    ↓ (for each task; parallelizable by dependency)\n  [CRITICAL: Requires Review Final (APPROVED) + Validation Final (APPROVED)]\n    ↓\nTASK_APPROVED (Architect)\n    ↓\n  [All tasks approved?]\n    ↓ (yes)\nCOMPLETED (Runner)\n\nAlternative paths:\n- Any draft → SUPERSEDED (requires new artifact + re-approval)\n- TASK_PENDING or TASK_IN_PROGRESS → BLOCKED (blocker must resolve)\n- TASK_PENDING or TASK_IN_PROGRESS → CANCELLED (removed from scope)\n```\n\n### State Definitions\n\n| State | Owner | Artifact | Condition |\n|-------|-------|----------|----------|\n| INITIATIVE_CREATED | Planner | Initiative | Draft complete; awaiting Architect review |\n| INITIATIVE_APPROVED | Architect | Initiative | Architect approved; Planning may commence |\n| PLAN_DRAFT | Planner | Plan | Plan drafted with phases, milestones, gates; awaiting review |\n| PLAN_REVIEWED | Reviewer | Plan | Reviewer assessed plan; awaiting Architect approval |\n| PLAN_APPROVED | Architect | Plan | Architect approved; Task Decomposer may create dependency-aware graph |\n| TASK_GRAPH_DRAFT | Task Decomposer | Task Graph | Graph drafted with all dependencies, parallelization; awaiting review |\n| TASK_GRAPH_REVIEWED | Reviewer | Task Graph | Reviewer assessed graph; awaiting Architect approval |\n| TASK_GRAPH_APPROVED | Architect | Task Graph | Architect approved dependencies; Executor may begin task execution |\n| TASK_PENDING | Executor | Task | Task created; dependencies met; awaiting execution start |\n| TASK_IN_PROGRESS | Executor | Task | Executor actively working; collecting evidence |\n| TASK_IMPLEMENTED | Executor | Task | Implementation complete, tests passed; awaiting Review + Validation + Architect approval |\n| TASK_APPROVED | Architect | Task | Architect approved after BOTH Review Final (APPROVED) AND Validation Final (APPROVED); task counts toward completion |\n| REVIEW_DRAFT | Reviewer | Review | Review drafted; awaiting Reviewer finalization |\n| REVIEW_FINAL | Reviewer | Review | Review complete; APPROVED or REJECTED decision binding |\n| VALIDATION_DRAFT | Validator | Validation | Validation tests drafted; awaiting finalization |\n| VALIDATION_FINAL | Validator | Validation | Validation complete; APPROVED or REJECTED decision binding |\n| COMPLETED | Runner | (Delivery) | All in-scope tasks Approved; all reviews/validations Final with APPROVED; no rejections |\n\n---\n\n## Agent Roles Table (Advanced Complexity — 8 Agent Roles + Runner)\n\n| Role | Responsibilities | Input | Output | Authority | Parallel? |\n|------|-----------------|-------|--------|------------|----------|\n| **Planner** | Create and refine Initiative and Plan artifacts; scope delivery, define phases/milestones | Requirement, constraints | Initiative (Draft), Plan (Draft) | Drafts; Architect approves | Sequential |\n| **Task Decomposer** | Break approved Plan into dependency-aware Task Graph; identify parallelizable branches | Approved Plan | Task Graph (Draft) | Drafts; Architect approves | Sequential |\n| **Implementation Planner** | Create scoped Implementation Plan with tests, rollback, evidence requirements | Approved Task | Implementation Plan (Draft) | Drafts; Architect approves | Per-task |\n| **Executor** | Implement approved tasks within scope; collect evidence; update Task state | Approved Task + Impl. Plan | Task (Implemented), code changes | Executes; Architect approves result | **By dependency DAG** |\n| **Reviewer** | Independent review of plans, graphs, implementations; contract compliance, bugs, scope drift | Task (Implemented) or Plan or Task Graph | Review (Draft → Final) | Drafts + finalizes; binding decision | Per-artifact |\n| **Validator** | Final behavior validation; acceptance criteria, contract compliance | Implementation + Review (Final) | Validation (Draft → Final) | Drafts + finalizes; binding decision | Per-task |\n| **Memory Manager** | Durable context, snapshots, supersession tracking, audit trail | Any artifact | Memory snapshots, linked artifacts | Maintains; Architect may request cleanup | Ongoing |\n| **Architect** | Workflow policy, approval gates, scope enforcement, exception routing | Any draft artifact | Approval or rejection + evidence | **Exclusive approval authority** for gates | Sequential gates |\n| **Runner** | State enforcement, budget, routing, sidecar validation, phase ordering | meta.json sidecars | Phase transitions, execution routing | Enforces SOP; blocks invalid transitions | State machine |\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Phases\n\n### Phase 1: Initiative\n\n**Owner**: Planner  \n**Agent**: Planner  \n**Input**: Requirement statement, constraint summary  \n**Action**:\n- Analyze requirement; define scope boundaries\n- Identify assumptions, risks, blockers, unknowns\n- Estimate effort, timeline, budget, model/coder preferences\n- Define success criteria (acceptance contract)\n- Draft Initiative artifact with structured metadata\n\n**Output**: `Initiative (Draft)` artifact in `01_initiatives/draft/` + meta.json sidecar  \n**Approval Gate**: Architect reviews; approves or rejects with evidence  \n**Next State**: INITIATIVE_APPROVED → PLAN_DRAFT  \n**Typical Duration**: 1-2 hours (human coders) or 15-30 min (automated agent)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Planning\n\n**Owner**: Planner  \n**Agent**: Planner  \n**Input**: Approved Initiative  \n**Action**:\n- Decompose Initiative into high-level phases, milestones, gates\n- Define delivery plan: what gets done when, by whom, in what order\n- Identify dependencies, critical path, parallelization opportunities\n- Define risk mitigation, contingencies, rollback strategy\n- Map success criteria → validation checkpoints\n- Create Plan artifact with phase details\n\n**Output**: `Plan (Draft)` artifact in `02_plans/` + meta.json sidecar  \n**Review Gate**: Reviewer assesses Plan for completeness and alignment (mandatory before Architect)  \n**Approval Gate**: Architect reviews; approves or rejects  \n**Next State**: PLAN_REVIEWED → PLAN_APPROVED → TASK_GRAPH_DRAFT  \n**Typical Duration**: 2-4 hours (human) or 30-60 min (automated)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Task Graph Creation\n\n**Owner**: Task Decomposer  \n**Agent**: Task Decomposer  \n**Input**: Approved Plan  \n**Action**:\n- Break Plan phases into concrete, executable tasks\n- Define task dependencies, parallelization, critical path\n- Estimate per-task effort, budget, timeout\n- Assign preferred coder/model per task (or \"any\", \"default\")\n- Create Task Graph artifact with DAG metadata\n- Register each task as individual Task artifact\n\n**Output**: `Task Graph (Draft)` artifact in `02_plans/artifacts/` + individual `Task (Pending)` artifacts + meta.json sidecars  \n**Review Gate**: Reviewer assesses Task Graph for dependencies and scope alignment (mandatory before Architect)  \n**Approval Gate**: Architect reviews dependencies, scope; approves or rejects  \n**Next State**: TASK_GRAPH_REVIEWED → TASK_GRAPH_APPROVED → TASK_PENDING (for each task)  \n**Typical Duration**: 1-3 hours (human) or 20-40 min (automated)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Task Execution (Parallelizable)\n\n**Owner**: Executor  \n**Agent**: Executor (may be multiple coders executing different tasks in parallel by dependency)  \n**Input**: Approved Task + Optional Approved Implementation Plan  \n**Action** (for each task, in dependency order):\n1. Read Approved Task artifact and sidecar\n2. Transition TASK_PENDING → TASK_IN_PROGRESS (runner verifies dependencies satisfied)\n3. Implement within approved scope (no drift, no scope expansion)\n4. Collect evidence: test results, hashes, logs, screen captures\n5. Update Task artifact with implementation details, code locations, evidence links\n6. Transition TASK_IN_PROGRESS → TASK_IMPLEMENTED (runner accepts sidecar)\n7. Request Reviewer to assess implementation\n\n**Output**: `Task (Implemented)` artifact + code changes + meta.json sidecar with evidence links  \n**Review Gate**: Reviewer independently assesses implementation (mandatory before Architect approval)  \n**Validation Gate**: Validator independently validates behavior (mandatory before Architect approval)  \n**Architect Approval Gate**: Architect approves ONLY after Review Final (APPROVED) AND Validation Final (APPROVED)  \n**Next State**: TASK_APPROVED (counts toward completion)  \n**Parallelization**: Multiple tasks may execute in parallel if dependencies permit. Runner enforces DAG order. Different coders may handle different tasks simultaneously.  \n**Typical Duration per Task**: 1-4 hours (human) or 15-60 min (automated), depending on complexity\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: Implementation Planning (Optional — Drafting Only)\n\n**Owner**: Implementation Planner  \n**Agent**: Implementation Planner  \n**Input**: Approved Task (or used inline with Phase 4)  \n**Clarity**: Drafting Implementation Plan is optional (may be inline with Task). However, if drafted, approval is **mandatory** before executor starts work.  \n**Action**:\n- Define scoped implementation steps (no scope expansion)\n- Outline test strategy (unit, integration, validation)\n- Define rollback plan (how to undo changes if needed)\n- Identify dependencies, blocking issues, known risks\n- Create Implementation Plan artifact\n\n**Output**: `Implementation Plan (Draft)` artifact in `04_implementation_plans/` + meta.json sidecar  \n**Approval Gate**: Architect reviews; approves or rejects (mandatory if plan is drafted)  \n**Next State**: IMPLEMENTATION_APPROVED → TASK_IN_PROGRESS (executor uses as reference)  \n**Optional Condition**: May skip drafting if Implementation is straightforward and Task definition suffices. However, approval (if drafted) is always mandatory before Executor begins work.  \n**Typical Duration**: 30 min - 1 hour (if needed)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 6: Review (Mandatory for Task Approval)\n\n**Owner**: Reviewer  \n**Agent**: Reviewer (must NOT be the executor; must be independent)  \n**Input**: Task (Implemented), approved code changes, test results  \n**Mandatory Requirement**: Review of implemented tasks is **mandatory before Task Approval**. Reviewer assessment is required for both Plan (Phase 2) and Task Graph (Phase 3) before Architect approval, and required for Tasks before final approval.  \n**Action**:\n- Independently review implementation against approved Plan/Task scope\n- Check contract compliance, code quality, test coverage\n- Identify bugs, regressions, scope drift, edge cases\n- Draft Review artifact with **structured findings** (see Review Decision Rule below)\n- Finalize with APPROVED or REJECTED decision + evidence\n\n**Output**: `Review (Final)` artifact in `05_reviews/` + meta.json sidecar with decision and findings  \n**Authority**: Reviewer drafts + finalizes; Architect may request revisions but Reviewer holds decision authority  \n**Next State**: REVIEW_FINAL → (Validation required before TASK_APPROVED)  \n**Typical Duration**: 1-2 hours (human) or 15-30 min (automated)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 7: Validation (Mandatory for Task Approval)\n\n**Owner**: Validator  \n**Agent**: Validator (must NOT be reviewer or executor; must be independent)  \n**Input**: Task (Implemented), Review (Final), deployed/staged code  \n**Mandatory Requirement**: Validation of implemented tasks is **mandatory before Task Approval**. Validator confirms behavior meets acceptance criteria.  \n**Action**:\n- Run final behavior/contract validation tests\n- Verify implementation meets success criteria from Initiative\n- Confirm no regressions, performance acceptable, contracts met\n- Draft and finalize Validation artifact with **structured findings** (see Validation Decision Rule below)\n- Include APPROVED or REJECTED decision + test results/evidence\n\n**Output**: `Validation (Final)` artifact in `05_reviews/` + meta.json sidecar with decision and evidence  \n**Authority**: Validator drafts + finalizes; Architect may request revisions but Validator holds decision authority  \n**Next State**: VALIDATION_FINAL (APPROVED) → TASK_APPROVED (after Architect gate)  \n**Typical Duration**: 2-4 hours (human) or 20-40 min (automated)\n\n---\n\n### Phase 8: Memory Management (Ongoing, Not Blocking)\n\n**Owner**: Memory Manager  \n**Agent**: Memory Manager  \n**Input**: All artifacts (Initiative, Plan, Task Graph, Task, Implementation Plan, Review, Validation)  \n**Action**:\n- Create periodic snapshots of delivery state after major gates\n- Track supersession links (old artifact → new artifact)\n- Maintain durable context (decisions, risks, constraints) for future workflows\n- Link related artifacts across workflow; build audit trail\n- Preserve hashes of approved artifacts for reproducibility\n\n**Output**: `Memory` artifacts in `06_memory/` + supersession metadata in all sidecars  \n**Authority**: Memory Manager maintains; Architect may request cleanup of stale memory  \n**Next State**: Ongoing; not blocking workflow completion  \n**Timing (Specific Memory Snapshot Triggers)**:\n  1. After Initiative Approved (record initial scope, constraints, success criteria)\n  2. After Plan Approved (record plan phases, milestones, dependencies)\n  3. After Task Graph Approved (record task breakdown, parallelization strategy)\n  4. After all Tasks Approved (record completion status, implementation evidence)\n  5. After Workflow Completed (record final delivery state, decisions, supersessions)\n**Typical Duration**: 15-30 min per snapshot\n\n---\n\n## Standard Rules (Non-Negotiable)\n\n### 1. Respect Current State\nNo agent may overwrite or skip a phase. Current state (from meta.json sidecar) determines next valid action. Runner enforces.\n\n### 2. No Phase Skipping\nPhases must execute in order: Initiative → Plan → Task Graph → Tasks → Review → Validation → Completed.\n\n### 3. No Overwriting Approved Artifacts\nOnce approved by authority (Architect, Reviewer, Validator), an artifact is locked. Changes require:\n- New artifact creation (with new ID)\n- Supersession link in metadata (old artifact: `\"superseded_by\": \"NEW-ID\"`; new artifact: `\"supersedes\": \"OLD-ID\"`)\n- Re-approval by same authority\n\n### 4. No Scope Drift\nExecutor may implement ONLY what Architect approved in the Task artifact. Scope expansion requires:\n- Escalation to Architect\n- New Task artifact or supersession of current Task\n- Re-approval before proceeding\n\n### 5. Deterministic Outputs\nEvery artifact must be deterministic: same input + same coder + same budget → same output (within model variance bounds). Artifact IDs are stable (YYYYMMDD-NN format).\n\n### 6. Single Source of Truth\nmeta.json sidecar is the ONLY communication channel between agents and runner. No fallback recovery, no stdout JSON parsing, no silent retries. Sidecar defines artifact status, approval decisions, and evidence.\n\n### 7. Document-First Execution\nNo step completes without:\n- Artifact body (markdown with required sections per template)\n- Folder placement (correct folder in docs/delivery/)\n- meta.json sidecar (schema v2, matching artifact ID)\n- Upstream linkage (references to dependencies)\n\nOrphaned code changes (without corresponding artifact) are invalid.\n\n### 8. Explicit Exception Routing\nFailures route immediately to Architect via `route_after_failure()`. No silencing, no recovery loops, no second tries without explicit re-invocation.\n\n### 9. Authority Is Durable\nOnce Architect approves a Task, that approval binds the Executor. Execution must not exceed approved scope. Approval is immutable; changes require new artifacts + re-approval.\n\n### 10. Multi-Coder + Multi-Model Support\nWorkflows dispatch tasks to different coders (Claude, Codex, Qwen) and different models (deepseek-chat, deepseek-reasoner, gpt-5.4-nano, qwen-claude, qwen-gemini).\n- Runner handles model alias resolution\n- Coder-specific CLI invocation\n- Budget enforcement per task\n- Timeout and retry logic per coder\n- Artifact must specify preferred coder/model (or \"any\"/\"default\")\n- Authority Precedence: Architect-specified > Template default > Runner default\n\n---\n\n## Forbidden Transitions (Strict Enforcement)\n\nThe runner will **reject** these state transitions:\n\n| Forbidden Transition | Reason |\n|---|---|\n| Initiative Draft → Completed | Must pass through Approved |\n| Initiative Draft → Approved (without sidecar) | Approval requires sidecar decision |\n| Plan Draft → Approved (without Review) | Review assessment mandatory before Architect approval |\n| Task Graph Draft → Approved (without Review) | Review assessment mandatory before Architect approval |\n| Task Pending → Implemented | Must pass through In Progress |\n| Task Pending → Approved | Must pass through In Progress, Implemented, Review, and Validation |\n| Task In Progress → Approved | Must pass through Implemented, Review, and Validation |\n| Task Implemented → Approved (without Review Final) | Review Final (APPROVED) mandatory before Architect approval |\n| Task Implemented → Approved (without Validation Final) | Validation Final (APPROVED) mandatory before Architect approval |\n| Task Implemented → Approved (Review or Validation REJECTED) | Rejection stops progression; workflow returns to execution phase |\n| Task Blocked → Implemented | Blocked tasks cannot progress until resolved |\n| Task Cancelled → any active state | Cancelled is terminal for that task |\n| Implementation Plan Draft → Execution | Must pass through Approved |\n| Review Draft → Workflow gate decision | Must be Final before affecting workflow |\n| Validation Draft → Workflow gate decision | Must be Final before affecting workflow |\n| Validation Rejected → Workflow COMPLETED | Rejection stops progression; cannot skip back |\n| Workflow COMPLETED (with rejected review/validation) | All reviews/validations must be Approved |\n| Workflow COMPLETED (with any Pending/In Progress task) | All in-scope tasks must be Approved |\n| Any approved artifact → Modified directly | Must supersede (create new version) |\n| Any superseded artifact → Used as active input | Must use latest version |\n| Any transition skipping phase | Phases must execute in order |\n| Any transition bypassing sidecar requirement | Sidecar is mandatory for state changes |\n\n---\n\n## Folder Structure\n\nDelivery artifacts are stored in `docs/delivery/` with the following standard layout:\n\n```\ndocs/delivery/\n├── 00_templates/\n│   ├── delivery_sop.json               # This SOP (schema v2 JSON)\n│   ├── delivery_status_rules.json      # Status rules (schema v2 JSON)\n│   ├── template_registry.md            # Document type mapping, templates, agent roles\n│   ├── AGENTS.md                       # Agent system overview\n│   ├── 01_initiative.template.md\n│   ├── 02_plan.template.md\n│   ├── 02b_task_graph.template.md\n│   ├── 03_task.template.md\n│   ├── 04_implementation_plan.template.md\n│   ├── 04_review.template.md\n│   ├── 05_validation.template.md\n│   ├── 06_memory.template.md\n│   └── 08_agents/\n│       ├── planner_contract.md\n│       ├── task_decomposer_contract.md\n│       ├── implementation_planner_contract.md\n│       ├── executor_contract.md\n│       ├── reviewer_contract.md\n│       ├── validator_contract.md\n│       └── memory_manager_contract.md\n│\n├── 01_initiatives/\n│   ├── draft/                          # Initiatives in progress\n│   │   └── INIT-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md\n│   └── pre_init/                       # Pre-initiative (requirements)\n│       └── *.meta.json\n│\n├── 02_plans/\n│   ├── PLAN-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md\n│   ├── PLAN-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│   └── artifacts/\n│       ├── TASK-GRAPH-YYYYMMDD-NN.md\n│       └── TASK-GRAPH-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│\n├── 03_tasks/\n│   ├── TASK-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md\n│   └── TASK-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│\n├── 04_implementation_plans/\n│   ├── IMPL-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md\n│   └── IMPL-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│\n├── 05_reviews/\n│   ├── REVIEW-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md        # Review artifacts\n│   ├── REVIEW-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│   ├── VALIDATION-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md    # Validation artifacts\n│   └── VALIDATION-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n│\n└── 06_memory/\n    ├── MEMORY-YYYYMMDD-NN_*.md\n    └── MEMORY-YYYYMMDD-NN.meta.json\n```\n\n**Do not create `07_master_prompts/`.** Agent master prompts are deprecated.\n\n---\n\n## Agent Contract File Specifications\n\nAgent contract files in `08_agents/` define role boundaries, input/output expectations, and handoff rules. Each contract must include:\n\n| Field | Requirement | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Role Name** | Required; matches role from SOP table | Identifies which agent this contract governs |\n| **Scope** | Required; explicit boundaries | What this agent can do; what is forbidden |\n| **Input Contract** | Required; artifact types and states | What artifact types/states trigger this agent |\n| **Output Contract** | Required; artifact types and structure | What this agent must produce (artifact type, folder, structure) |\n| **Authority Boundaries** | Required; approval authority | What this agent can approve vs. what requires Architect gate |\n| **Handoff Rules** | Required; downstream expectations | How outputs connect to downstream agents |\n| **Constraints** | Required; budget, scope, timing | Time limits, budget limits, scope constraints, no-drift rules |\n\n**Agent contracts define boundaries ONLY, not prompt content.** Agent master prompts are deprecated. Invocation details are in `template_groups.py` workflow step configurations.\n\n**Required Contract Files:**\n- `planner_contract.md` — Planner role scope, Initiative/Plan inputs and outputs\n- `task_decomposer_contract.md` — Task Decomposer scope, Plan→Task Graph transformation rules\n- `implementation_planner_contract.md` — Implementation Planner scope, Task→Implementation Plan rules\n- `executor_contract.md` — Executor scope, approved task execution constraints, no-drift rules\n- `reviewer_contract.md` — Reviewer role scope, review independence, decision authority\n- `validator_contract.md` — Validator role scope, validation independence, contract verification\n- `memory_manager_contract.md` — Memory Manager scope, snapshot triggers, supersession tracking\n\n---\n\n## Review and Validation Decision Rule\n\n**Every Review and Validation artifact must record structured decisions with these required fields:**\n\n| Field | Requirement | Details |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Target** | Artifact ID, version, path | Exactly what is being reviewed (e.g., PLAN-20260603-01, TASK-20260603-02) |\n| **Decision** | APPROVED or REJECTED | Binding decision; determines workflow routing |\n| **Findings** | Structured observations | Organized by severity (Critical, Major, Minor); include issue description, location, impact |\n| **Evidence** | Tests, hashes, logs, references | Concrete proof supporting the decision (test results, code reviews, contract checks, performance metrics) |\n| **Follow-up** | Corrections required, owner, routing | If rejected, specify what must be fixed, who fixes it, where workflow returns |\n\n**Decision Binding:**\n- **APPROVED:** Workflow advances to next phase (if both Review and Validation approved)\n- **REJECTED:** Workflow routes back to Executor for corrections (findings specify what must be fixed)\n\nApproval is effective **only after runner accepts the sidecar**. Decision in artifact body is advisory; decision in sidecar is authoritative.\n\n---\n\n## Validation Philosophy\n\n### Independent\nReview and Validation are performed by agents independent of implementation. Reviewer does not execute; Validator does not review.\n\n### Structured\nValidation is not narrative. Every finding must include:\n- **Target**: What was checked (artifact ID, code file, test)\n- **Decision**: Pass / Conditional / Fail\n- **Finding**: Specific issue (or confirmation of compliance)\n- **Evidence**: Test output, hash, log, screenshot, citation\n- **Follow-up**: Action required or cleared\n\n### Mandatory Before Completion\nNo workflow may complete (COMPLETED state) without:\n- All in-scope tasks in TASK_APPROVED state\n- Review (Final) with APPROVED decision (mandatory for all implemented tasks)\n- Validation (Final) with APPROVED decision (mandatory for all implemented tasks)\n- All approval decisions signed in meta.json sidecars with evidence\n- No rejected reviews or validations\n\n### Contract-Driven\nValidation checks **success criteria** defined in the Initiative or Plan. Validator confirms delivery meets stated contract.\n\n---\n\n## Communication Protocol: meta.json Sidecar\n\n**CRITICAL: meta.json is the only communication channel between agents and runner.**\n\n### No Pre-Invocation Writes\nThe runner does NOT write meta.json sidecars before invoking an agent. Agents are responsible for creating/updating sidecars as they complete work.\n\n### No Markdown Write-Backs\nNo `sync_review_metadata`, no `stamp_created_metadata`, no sidecar-to-markdown sync. Sidecar is the single source of truth.\n\n### Explicit Exception Routing\nOn failure, the runner invokes `route_after_failure()` immediately. No silent recovery. No fallback. Explicit routing to Architect.\n\n### Sidecar Structure (Schema v2 — Complete)\n\nEvery artifact includes a **durable sidecar** at `<artifact-basename>.meta.json`. The complete schema v2:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"v2\",\n  \"coder_result\": {\n    \"status\": \"Draft | Reviewed | Approved | Final | Implemented | Completed | Superseded | Cancelled\",\n    \"decision\": true | false,\n    \"remark\": \"Brief summary of result\",\n    \"artifacts\": {\n      \"artifact_name\": \"/absolute/path/to/file\",\n      \"other_artifact\": \"/absolute/path/to/file2\"\n    },\n    \"findings\": [\n      {\n        \"severity\": \"Critical | Major | Minor\",\n        \"issue\": \"Description\",\n        \"location\": \"File:line or section\",\n        \"impact\": \"What breaks or degrades\",\n        \"follow_up\": \"Action required or cleared\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"test_result | hash | log | screenshot | code_review\",\n        \"path\": \"/absolute/path\",\n        \"hash_sha256\": \"hex_string_or_null\",\n        \"notes\": \"Context for this evidence\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"upstream_refs\": [\"INIT-YYYYMMDD-NN\", \"PLAN-YYYYMMDD-NN\"],\n    \"supersedes\": null | \"OLD-ID\",\n    \"superseded_by\": null | \"NEW-ID\",\n    \"recorded_at\": \"2026-06-03T10:30:00Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Schema Field Requirements:**\n- **schema_version**: Must be \"v2\" (string)\n- **status**: Valid state for artifact type (string)\n- **decision**: Required for approval gates (boolean: true=approved, false=rejected)\n- **remark**: Brief human-readable summary (string)\n- **artifacts**: Map of artifact names to absolute file paths (object; all paths must exist)\n- **findings**: Optional; required for review/validation artifacts (array of objects with severity, issue, location, impact, follow_up)\n- **evidence**: Optional; required for review/validation artifacts with findings (array of objects with type, path, hash_sha256, notes)\n- **upstream_refs**: List of artifact IDs this depends on (array of strings; enables traceability)\n- **supersedes/superseded_by**: Artifact linkage for version control (string or null)\n- **recorded_at**: ISO 8601 timestamp (string; immutable once written)\n\n---\n\n## Execution Discipline\n\n### Runner as State Enforcer\n1. Runner reads artifact status from meta.json sidecar\n2. Runner enforces SOP state transitions (rejects invalid jumps)\n3. Runner blocks phases out of order\n4. Runner routes failures immediately via `route_after_failure()`\n5. Runner validates sidecar schema, artifact linkage, upstream refs\n6. Runner logs all state changes (audit trail)\n\n### Agent as Executor\n1. Agent reads approved artifact + sidecar (read-only context)\n2. Agent performs work within scope (no drift)\n3. Agent writes output artifact + updated sidecar\n4. Agent does NOT approve own work (Architect/Reviewer/Validator approves)\n5. Agent reports completion via sidecar; runner/Architect advances state\n\n### Architect as Gatekeeper\n1. Architect reads draft artifact + sidecar\n2. Architect reviews against contract, scope, quality, risk\n3. Architect updates sidecar with approval/rejection decision + evidence\n4. Architect provides remark (brief summary)\n5. Architect's decision is durable and binding (cannot be reversed without supersession)\n\n---\n\n## Supersession and Artifact Lifecycle\n\nWhen an approved artifact must be replaced:\n\n1. **New artifact is created** with new ID (YYYYMMDD-NN format)\n2. **Supersession link is recorded** in both sidecars:\n   - Old artifact sidecar: `\"superseded_by\": \"NEW-ARTIFACT-ID\"`\n   - New artifact sidecar: `\"supersedes\": \"OLD-ARTIFACT-ID\"`\n3. **Old artifact remains on disk** (immutable; audit trail)\n4. **New artifact requires re-approval** by same authority\n5. **Executor uses only new artifact** (runner blocks use of superseded artifacts)\n\n**Implication**: Changing scope is auditable and requires re-approval. No silent modifications.\n\n---\n\n## Backward Compatibility & Daemon Mode\n\n**Direct Execution (v1 - Preserved):**\n- CLI invocation without daemon\n- Single-threaded synchronous execution\n- Fully supported and unchanged\n- SOP rules apply equally\n\n**Daemon Mode (Planned, Future):**\n- Asynchronous job queuing\n- PostgreSQL-backed job management (agent_runner_v2.db.job_metadata)\n- Multi-worker support\n- Does NOT change core SOP rules\n- State machine and approval gates remain binding\n\n---\n\n## Related Documents & Specifications\n\n- **DELIVERY_STATUS_RULES_v1.md** — Artifact lifecycle, approval gates, forbidden transitions, authority model\n- **UKBE_Artifact_v1_FINAL.md** — Artifact structure and determinism requirements\n- **UKBE_Contract_Builder_v1.1_FINAL.md** — Contract freeze workflow and budget enforcement\n- **UKBE_Core_Data_Model_v1.2.1_FINAL.md** — Canonical internal data structures\n- **template_registry.md** — Index of all delivery templates and document types\n- **08_agents/AGENTS.md** — Agent system overview and role contracts\n- **template_groups.py** — Workflow step configurations (agent contracts for invocation)\n- **pyproject.toml** — Runner configuration, model mappings, CLI entry points\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThis SOP establishes **explicit, enforceable, document-driven delivery**. No ambiguity. No silent recovery. No scope drift. Every phase is accountable to the state machine, every decision is durable in the sidecar, every approval is binding. The runner enforces these rules. The Architect approves within these rules. The Executor works within these rules. The result is reproducible, auditable, and safe at scale."
}
